# Drain Power: "Target player activates a mana ability of each land they control. Then that player loses all unspent mana
# and you add the mana lost this way." (CR 117.2e, 605.3a, 106.4). Bot2 controls an Island, a Shivan Reef (two mana
# abilities: Bot2 chooses the {U} or {R} one, red, and takes its 1 damage - the 2004-10-04 ruling that the target player
# chooses) and a Forest tapped on its own turn, which has no mana ability it can activate and is skipped (CR 609.3). The
# Island was tapped for mana on an earlier turn and has untapped since: only an activation during Drain Power's own
# instruction counts toward it, so it is still owed. In
# response Bot2 taps Mox Ruby, which is no land: its {R} is not asked for, but it is unspent mana, lost with the rest; Mox
# Jet, no land either, is never asked for and stays untapped. Bot1
# ends with {U}{R}{R}, its own two untapped Islands untouched; Bot2's pool is empty. Losing the mana before the activations
# would leave Bot2 holding the lands' {U}{R}, so the order is shown too.

